Patch: OpenGLide-ng 64-bit, read-only-install and continuous fog fixes
Upstream: https://github.com/eugenenuke/openglide-ng at the commit named by BACKEND in tools/package_native.py; applied by tools/build_glide.py and tools/build_linux.py.
Original: FindConfig reads its configuration file without checking that it opened; GetOptions writes OpenGLid.ini unchecked and recurses if it cannot remove a bad file; RDTSC reads the timestamp counter with the 32-bit "=A" constraint, which is wrong on x86-64. OGLFogDistance rounds depth up to the next fog-table entry, so small camera or water-vertex movements abruptly change a whole triangle's fog density.
Replacement: FindConfig returns when the file is missing; GetOptions logs "Cannot write wrapper configuration; using defaults" and returns, and only recurses if the bad file was removed; RDTSC assembles the 64-bit value from EAX and EDX. OGLFogDistance interpolates adjacent densities in reciprocal depth and retains endpoint clamping.
Effect: the renderer starts when the game directory is read-only (the native build mounts it read-only), its timing counter is correct on 64-bit, and distant fog no longer jumps at table boundaries. Fog remains calculated per vertex; this does not implement the original hardware's per-pixel fog or dithering.
Why: the game is run from an unmodified, possibly read-only installation, and the build is 64-bit. Glide interpolates fog in reciprocal depth; stepping between table entries produces moving dark bands on the opening ship's water.
Evidence: tests/backend_smoke.cpp checks rendered white triangles against black fog across the distant-water thresholds, at an interior depth, with falling densities and outside the table range. Before the fog fix, moving from depth 2730.650 to 2730.680 changed the captured red channel from 115 to 57. The opening-ship band persists with waves frozen or flattened and disappears with fog disabled in native Linux software-GL probes; this is not hardware or real-Windows acceptance. The Glide window checks exercise startup in Linux and Wine.

diff --git a/GLutil.cpp b/GLutil.cpp
index 8cef475..e009e09 100644
--- a/GLutil.cpp
+++ b/GLutil.cpp
@@ -232,6 +232,7 @@ static char * FindConfig( const char *IniFile, const char *IniConfig )
 
     Find = NULL;
     file = fopen( IniFile, "r" );
+    if (!file) return NULL;
 
     while ( fgets( Buffer1, 255, file ) != NULL )
     {
@@ -297,6 +298,10 @@ void GetOptions( void )
     if ( access( Path, 0 ) == -1 )
     {
         IniFile = fopen( Path, "w" );
+        if (!IniFile) {
+            GlideMsg("Cannot write wrapper configuration; using defaults\n");
+            return;
+        }
         fprintf( IniFile, "Configuration File for OpenGLide\n\n" );
         fprintf( IniFile, "Info:\n" );
         fprintf( IniFile, "Priority goes from 0(HIGH) to 5(IDLE)\n" );
@@ -372,8 +377,7 @@ void GetOptions( void )
         }
         else
         {
-            remove( Path );
-            GetOptions( );
+            if (remove( Path ) == 0) GetOptions( );
         }
     }
 }
diff --git a/GlOgl.h b/GlOgl.h
index 1185a91..dd50b57 100644
--- a/GlOgl.h
+++ b/GlOgl.h
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifdef __GNUC__
-#define RDTSC(v)    asm volatile ("rdtsc;" : "=A" (v) )
+#define RDTSC(v) do { unsigned lo, hi; asm volatile ("rdtsc" : "=a" (lo), "=d" (hi)); (v) = ((FxU64)hi << 32) | lo; } while (0)
 #endif
 
 #define ERRORFILE               "OpenGLid.err"
diff --git a/OGLFogTables.cpp b/OGLFogTables.cpp
--- a/OGLFogTables.cpp
+++ b/OGLFogTables.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,18 @@
 {
-    int i;
-    for (i = 0; ((i < GR_FOG_TABLE_SIZE) && (tableIndexToW[i] < w)); i++);
-    i = (i == GR_FOG_TABLE_SIZE)? (GR_FOG_TABLE_SIZE - 1):i;
-    return Glide.FogTable[i] * D1OVER255;
+    int upper;
+    for (upper = 0; upper < GR_FOG_TABLE_SIZE && tableIndexToW[upper] < w; ++upper);
+    if (upper == 0)
+        return Glide.FogTable[0] * D1OVER255;
+    if (upper == GR_FOG_TABLE_SIZE)
+        return Glide.FogTable[GR_FOG_TABLE_SIZE - 1] * D1OVER255;
+
+    // Glide's fog-table fraction is linear in reciprocal depth, not distance.
+    // Looking up only the next entry makes water triangles pop as they move.
+    const int lower = upper - 1;
+    const float nearReciprocal = 1.0f / tableIndexToW[lower];
+    const float farReciprocal = 1.0f / tableIndexToW[upper];
+    const float fraction = (nearReciprocal - 1.0f / w) /
+                           (nearReciprocal - farReciprocal);
+    return (Glide.FogTable[lower] +
+            fraction * (Glide.FogTable[upper] - Glide.FogTable[lower])) * D1OVER255;
 }
